new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5af455d9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/slices/bounded-inference.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Bounded inference on the owning Runtime
+
+The consumer needs its existing text, images, structured TypeSafe judgments and local inference to share one Runtime and Host. No App model HTTP fallback or second runtime is allowed.
+
+Text remains Session.startRun with ephemeral sessions and no workspace root. Model parsers emit bounded provider-reported model identity separately from requested identity. Images retain the existing ImageSurface, model adapters, credential references, Host network gate, usage ledger and resource refs. Add Gemini, URL results fetched by Host without forwarding model credentials, signal cancellation and configured response/image bounds. Explicit auth-none is restricted to permitted loopback model endpoints. Native TypeSafe uses a structured model adapter and bounded Runtime composition surface; state/questions/results remain native JSON, never a natural-language prompt. Local engines must execute through a Prologue-owned Host process boundary with cancellation and receipts; exact process contract will be recorded before implementation.
+
+Hard boundaries: Host owns networking, credentials, processes and file access; App selects endpoint/model, request input, bounds and user consent. Adapter code only translates protocols. Configuration lives under existing module config. Runtime shutdown cancels active inference. Invalid/empty/over-limit outputs and changed credentials never publish a successful consumer result.
+
+Validation: real Node Host loopback text/OpenAI images/Gemini/TypeSafe, safe errors, abort during I/O, auth-none loopback and remote denial, image URL isolation and byte limits, resource receipt reads. Then packed SDK production consumer integration and configured model execution. Existing Action identity/budget/approval behavior remains unchanged.
+
+## Trusted Agent scopes: no workspace and owned Builder sessions
+
+The coordinating App owner authorizes a pure-inference role to run on the existing durable Session without a filesystem root. Extend existing Runtime.startAgentRun with explicit workspace: "none" (default remains required). This branch forbids rootRef, native/system/custom/MCP/Action/subagent tools, active pack tool contributions and workspace context; toolNames must be explicit empty. It preserves Character/persona, mounted text resources, history, model/usage, budgets, before-dispatch guard, same AgentLoop/Session ledger and cancellation/control. Never synthesize an authorized root or read cwd/home project files. Existing workspace Agents retain original behavior.
+
+Builder needs positive allow only within its own trusted Session, on an already authorized root. Extend the existing Session/Run permission contract or another existing frozen authority input with trusted session-scoped grants; no global allow rule. Freeze exact Session/Run/root into the existing effect-chain policy evaluation. Organizational/project deny, sandbox/authorized-root restrictions and later deny hooks still win. Grant can allow the bounded tool names and authorized-root paths; App's session-filtered hook further narrows writes to allowed builder files. Tool registration/execution remains existing Session pack mechanism. Other simultaneous Coding sessions must retain their original approvals. Validate with real Node Host two concurrent Sessions and negative policy/host cases.
+
+### Public Agent scope API and boundaries
+
+`Runtime.startAgentRun({ workspace: "none", session, start, agent: { toolNames: [], ... }, history: "session" })` uses the same AgentLoop, resource binding, Character, control, usage and durable Session ledger. It does not construct a workspace reader or mutator. Default/`workspace: "required"` still requires a real root. A no-workspace call rejects roots in either start shape, per-Run tool executors, contributed Session pack tools, Character tools/skills/MCP, subagents, workspace context, and a missing/nonempty toolNames list. Window/compaction options remain available.
+
+Rooted calls may provide trusted App `grants: { toolNames, paths }`. This slice supports paths `[]` or `["."]` only: authorize the actual build directory as its own Host root; a child directory string is rejected because lexical path matching cannot provide canonical symlink isolation. Grants are copied before the first await and never persisted or inherited. A private capability binds the grant to exact Session/Run/root, namespaces effect identities and checks authority on cached preparation and dispatch, including after Host dispatch preparation. All explicit denies, unknown effects, escalation, sandbox and final Host checks remain stronger; tool-before hooks may still narrow. Commands and network receive no implicit grant. Read tool policy denies are checked before execution.
+
+Validation: `pnpm exec vitest run packages/sdk/test/agent-scopes.live.test.ts` uses a real Node Host, local HTTP model transport and actual files for no-root Character/material/history/usage/dispatch-guard/budget/abort behavior, zero workspace calls, contradictory input rejection, concurrent Builder/Coding approval isolation, two granted Session pack executors, global/hook/sandbox/root denials, scoped replay and dispatch spoof rejection, and rejected child path grants. `pnpm build` checks the public package.
